<title>ITALY: Specialists get 50 bln lire of Italy 5-yr BTPs.</title>
<headline>Specialists get 50 bln lire of Italy 5-yr BTPs.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Specialist bond traders bid for and were allocated 50 billion lire of five-year fixed-rate bonds (BTP) against the Italian Treasury's offer of 250 billion lire of paper.</p>
<p>Earlier, the Treasury received bids for 4.691 trillion lire at the open auction for the March 1, 2002 paper, against 2.5 trillion lire worth of paper on offer.</p>
<p>The auction price was set at 97.75 from 94.80 at the previous sale on March 28.</p>
</text>
